ENTRY            C2833   20260717   20261014   20261014       C259
SUBENT        C2833001   20260717   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                 11         29
TITLE      Investigation of direct capture in the 23Na(p,gamma)
           24Mg reaction
AUTHOR     (A.Boeltzig,R.J.deBoer,Y.Chen,A.Best,M.Couder,
           A.Di Leva,B.Frentz,J.Gorres,Gy.Gyurky,G.Imbriani,
           M.Junker,Q.Liu,S.Lyons,K.Manukyan,K.T.Macon,
           L.Morales,M.T.Moran,D.Odell,C.Seymour,G.Seymour,
           E.Stech,B.Vande Kolk,M.Wiescher)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,106,045801,2022)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.106.045801
INSTITUTE  (2ITYNAP,1USANOT,3HUNDEB,2ITYLGS,1USAOHO)
FACILITY   (ACCEL,1USANOT) The Stable ion Accelerator for
           Nuclear Astrophysics (Sta. ANA), a 5 MV single-ended
           Pelletron accelerator.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) The detector system consisted of a single,
           high efficiency (120% relative efficiency), high
           purity, co-axial germanium detector (HPGe).
SAMPLE     Targets were produced by evaporating Na2WO4 onto a
           0.5 mm thick Ta backing, which also served as a beam
           stop, and which was electrically isolated from the
           rest of the beam line.
METHOD     (GSPEC) Measurements of the 23Na(p,gamma)24Mg cross
           section were taken in close geometry.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No details on sources of uncertainties.
CORRECTION The detector was mounted on a rail system at an angle
           of 45 degree relative to the beam. The rail system
           allowed the detector to be easily moved to different
           distances from the target in order to make summing
           correction measurements during the calibration.
HISTORY    (20260717C) BP
ENDBIB              29
